CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*region)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct vfio_region_zpci_io)...)
#307: FILE: drivers/vfio/pci/vfio_pci_zdev.c:281:
+	region = kmalloc(sizeof(struct vfio_region_zpci_io), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

